    "https://centrecollege.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/Centre/job/Danville-Kentucky/Assistant-Director-of-Student-Activities-for-Greek-Life_JR100246": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Activities for Greek Life",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJoin Centre College as we recruit exceptional faculty and staff! At Centre, we seek passionate and qualified individuals committed to fostering academic excellence, vibrant community, and inclusive growth. We offer competitive compensation, comprehensive benefits, and ongoing professional development. Our collegial environment values diversity of perspectives, encourages meaningful discourse and celebrates the unique contributions of each community member. The Assistant Director of Student Activities for Greek Life and Operations has responsibility for advising Fraternity & Sorority Councils and chapter support while overseeing student organization operational systems, reservations, student staffing operations, and designated Student Life managed facilities. They are a member of the Student Life staff team under the direction of the Director of Student Activities and Greek Life. Please submit resume/CV and cover letter with application.   Essential Job Functions: Fraternity and Sorority Life Support • Advise eleven inter/national chapters; • Advise Order of Omega and Gamma Sigma Alpha honoraries; • Advise the Panhellenic and Interfraternity Councils; • Oversee Greek Recruitment and Greek Accreditation program for Chapter Recognition; • Administer College policies, procedures, and guidelines that apply to campus organizations and event management; • Support risk management, leadership development, Greek programs, and educational initiatives within the fraternity and sorority community.   Student Organization Operations • Oversee student organization operational processes including event registration systems, reservation processes, and organizational compliance initiatives; • Coordinate space reservations and operational support for designated Student Life managed spaces.     Roush Campus Center and Combs Warehouse Operations • Oversee the management and daily operations of the Roush Campus Center, Combs Warehouse, outdoor student life venues, other areas of campus managed by the Student Activities and Greek Life Office including the event reservation system, room setup operations, and facility coordination; • Train, supervise, and oversee student workers for the Roush Campus Center; • Supervise operational support and facility readiness for Student Life managed spaces.   Other Student Life Duties • Oversee shuttle program for student arrival and departure during campus breaks; • Assist with student transition support initiatives; • Participate in Student Life staff meetings, regular individual meetings with supervisors, and the annual Student Life staff retreat; • Assist on special projects; participate as a team member in all aspects of Student Life; • Demonstrate an appreciation for and sensitivity to an inclusive academic community, fostering a welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff from all social, economic, cultural, ideological, racial, and ethnic backgrounds; • Contribute to the overall success of the department by performing all other essential duties and responsibilities as assigned.   Requirements: Education • Master’s Degree in Higher Education Administration, College Student Personnel, Counseling, or related field preferred; or an equivalent combination of education and experience.   Knowledge and Skills • Willing to work flexible schedule, which will include evening and weekend hours as required to meet with student organizations and to facilitate activities; • Excellent oral and written communication skills, organization skills, and the ability to manage multiple tasks; • Knowledge of NIC and NPC structures and policies; • Experience with event operations, reservations systems, student staffing, and facility management preferred.   Physical Requirements Limited pushing, pulling, lifting. Lifting would not exceed 50 lbs. Mobility on campus necessary. Centre provides a supportive, engaging setting where faculty and staff thrive as we advance our shared mission: preparing students for lives of learning, leadership, and service. Join our community and leave a lasting impact on generations to come. As a fundamental policy and in compliance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and all other applicable non-discrimination laws, Centre College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression, age, disability, veteran’s status, or genetic information in the administration of any of its education or employment policies. Centre College hires and promotes its employees and admits its students on the basis of merit, qualification, and character."
    },
    "https://centrecollege.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/Centre/job/Danville-Kentucky/Associate-or-Assistant-Athletic-Trainer_JR100006": {
      "title": "Associate or Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Centre College as we recruit exceptional faculty and staff! At Centre, we seek passionate and qualified individuals committed to fostering academic excellence, vibrant community, and inclusive growth. We offer competitive compensation, comprehensive benefits, and ongoing professional development. Our collegial environment values diversity of perspectives, encourages meaningful discourse and celebrates the unique contributions of each community member. Centre College is seeking qualified applicants for a position of Associate or Assistant Athletic Trainer.     As a key member of Centre College Sports Medicine Team, the Athletic Trainer will be an active part in the five domains of athletic training: prevention of athletic injuries, recognition, evaluation and immediate care of athletic injuries, rehabilitation and reconditioning of athletic injuries, health care administration and professional development and responsibility. Start date is negotiable with opportunities to work various sports camps on campus in June and July.  This is a full time, 10-month position; Varies depending on workload and season, will include evenings, weekends, and overnight travel. Centre College is a DIII school with an athletics block scheduled from 4-7pm. Come join our amazing staff of lifelong learners and motivated coworkers. These positions report to the Head Athletic Trainer / Athletic Healthcare Administrator.  This position will provide comprehensive healthcare and injury prevention services for: 1.     AT Position #1: Football, Baseball, Men’s & Women’s Tennis 2.     AT Position #2: Football, Men’s & Women’s Cross Country and Track & Field, Cheer Please indicate in your cover letter if you are applying for the Football/Baseball AT or Football/XCTF AT position. You may indicate if you are interested in both positions.  Essential Job Functions Evaluation, treatment and rehabilitation of athletic injuries Provides practice and competition coverage of assigned teams, and assists other teams as needed. Travel as needed with assigned teams Appropriate use of therapeutic modalities, taping, and bracing Proactive identification and management of concussions in conjunction with team physician Completes necessary documentation using Sportsware EMR Collaborates with strength and conditioning staff, team physician, student health, and all other members of health care team regarding student-athlete care Clearly communicates with coaching staff regarding injuries and treatment plans Maintain CPR/First Aid for professional rescuer certification Relates necessary sports medicine information to visiting institutions and athletic training staff Daily operation and maintenance of athletic training facilities Administrative duties as assigned by Head Athletic Trainer Abides by rules set forth by both NCAA, state of Kentucky, and SAA conference Maintain continuing education according to the requirements of BOC and state of Kentucky Demonstrate an appreciation for and sensitivity to an inclusive academic community, fostering a welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff from all social, economic, cultural, ideological, racial, and ethnic backgrounds Qualifications Master’s Degree preferred, Bachelor's degree required.  BOC certification in good standing License from the Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure First Aid/CPR certification for the Professional Rescuer NPI Number Preferred Must be able to pass a background check Excellent verbal and written communication skills Effective team player Ability to react appropriately in emergency situations per state licensure guidelines Decision-Making Skills: Ability to think critically and make independent decisions regarding assessment, treatment, rehabilitation and return to play decisions Additional certifications and skills, including but not limited to: Graston, ART, Cupping, Dry Needling, CSCS, CES, etc. are beneficial        Physical Requirements Moderate physical activity and standing or walking for several hours per day Lifting and handling of moderately heavy objects (water, ice-chests, etc.) is expected (25-40lbs) Centre provides a supportive, engaging setting where faculty and staff thrive as we advance our shared mission: preparing students for lives of learning, leadership, and service. Join our community and leave a lasting impact on generations to come. As a fundamental policy and in compliance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and all other applicable non-discrimination laws, Centre College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression, age, disability, veteran’s status, or genetic information in the administration of any of its education or employment policies. Centre College hires and promotes its employees and admits its students on the basis of merit, qualification, and character."
    },
    "https://centrecollege.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/Centre/job/Danville-Kentucky/Custodian_JR100041-1": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Centre College as we recruit exceptional faculty and staff! At Centre, we seek passionate and qualified individuals committed to fostering academic excellence, vibrant community, and inclusive growth. We offer competitive compensation, comprehensive benefits, and ongoing professional development. Our collegial environment values diversity of perspectives, encourages meaningful discourse and celebrates the unique contributions of each community member. Perform work covering all phases of custodial maintenance for the College according to standards set forth, care of equipment and economical use of all supplies. Essential Job Functions: Reports to a Custodial Leader who is responsible for the direction of the custodial operations for a given facility; Clean and service buildings - dusting, sweeping and mopping rooms, halls, laboratories and stairwells; Strips, scrubs, applies finishes and spray buff floors; Clean bathrooms, laboratories, fixtures and polishes brass, chrome, and stainless steel using established practices and procedures; Gathers and disposes refuse; Washes walls, windows (exterior and interior) and shampoos carpets; Cleans lighting fixtures, replacing light bulbs, tops of windows, door frames and other high areas using ladders of various heights; Refills paper product dispensers; Maintains cleanliness and order in the custodial storage area; Lock and unlock assigned buildings, secure building when facility is not in use checking for unlocked doors and windows, report any unauthorized occupants; Perform cleaning and related activities such as removing snow or debris from entrances, stairs in areas within six feet of buildings using shovels, brooms, and ice melting chemicals; Attend to emergencies when necessary; Assist with inventory control and security of assigned building(s); Safely operate all job-related equipment; Secure storage areas; Maintain a 10ft perimeter around the exterior of all buildings, including but not limited to trash, leaves in the exterior stairwell and entryways, branches on sidewalk, snow removal, etc.; Duties require outside transferring of trash to dumpster in inclement weather conditions; Ensure cleaning materials and supplies are stored in a safe, orderly, and secure manner; Enforce and adhere to Standard Safety precautions and attend all mandatory training; Facilities Management provides critical services to the college to ensure the safety of the students, faculty, and staff.  Facilities employees are critical personnel, which requires us to be present during inclement weather and all other emergencies. Marginal Job Functions: Occasionally assists in moving freight and furniture; May be required to make minor repairs to equipment; Requests supplies as needed; Contribute to the overall success of the department by performing all other essential duties and responsibilities as assigned. Education and Experience High School diploma or equivalent combination of education and experience.  Previous experience is preferred. Individual will learn duties through the job training. Knowledge and Skills Must know how to use common house cleaning devices such as brooms, mops, etc.  Familiar with physical arrangement of buildings, electrical, water locations and fire alarms, and standard procedures for cleaning walls, floors, etc. Ability to work with due consideration for faculty, staff and students in vicinity. Demonstrates initiative in assessing and maintaining appropriate cleaning standards.  Works under relatively close supervision, performing simple and standardized tasks.  Maintains professional appearance and conduct, demonstrating integrity and accountability in a student-facing environment and when entrusted with institutional property. Maintains a regular work schedule and is available to work overtime as needed. Physical Requirements: The job involves all of the following in various degrees but is not limited to only these physical demands:  carrying, standing, pulling, pushing, turning, stooping, lifting, squatting, sitting, climbing stairs and ladders, walking, kneeling, cleaning, reaching, crawling, twisting and writing. Must be able to lift up to 50 lbs. independently. Also involves exposure to the following environmental conditions: fumes, oil, dirt, hazards, gas, chemicals, heat/cold, toxins and noise. Centre provides a supportive, engaging setting where faculty and staff thrive as we advance our shared mission: preparing students for lives of learning, leadership, and service. Join our community and leave a lasting impact on generations to come. As a fundamental policy and in compliance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and all other applicable non-discrimination laws, Centre College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression, age, disability, veteran’s status, or genetic information in the administration of any of its education or employment policies. Centre College hires and promotes its employees and admits its students on the basis of merit, qualification, and character."
    },
    "https://centrecollege.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/Centre/job/Danville-Kentucky/HVAC-Technician_JR100009": {
      "title": "HVAC Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Centre College as we recruit exceptional faculty and staff! At Centre, we seek passionate and qualified individuals committed to fostering academic excellence, vibrant community, and inclusive growth. We offer competitive compensation, comprehensive benefits, and ongoing professional development. Our collegial environment values diversity of perspectives, encourages meaningful discourse and celebrates the unique contributions of each community member. Assists in the general operations and maintenance of the mechanical, HVAC and associated systems to accomplish a smooth operating environment for all faculty, staff and students. Starting pay for this position is $28.85 per hour.   Essential Job Functions Under the general supervision of the Maintenance Superintendent, reads and records operating characteristics of various heating, air conditioning, and gas distribution systems; Service and maintain HVAC systems including use and management of CFC compounds; Performs maintenance to all aspects of building operating systems; Assists in performing audits of all equipment and establishing and completing preventive maintenance programs; Troubleshoots and makes repairs to operating equipment, all controls and control equipment associated with building operating systems; Assists in installation, connection/disconnecting of various electrical devices, all voltages and performs troubleshooting of all type of electrical lines and equipment, as refers to HVAC equipment; Services and maintains the emergency powered generators; Serves as an on-call person for designated periods to respond to emergencies after normal working hours; In compliance with the Facilities Management On-Call and Overtime Policies.   Enforce and adhere to standard safety precautions.  Attend all mandatory training; Demonstrate an appreciation for and sensitivity to a diverse academic community, fostering an inclusive environment for students, faculty, and staff from a variety of social, economic, cultural, ideological, racial, and ethnic backgrounds. Facilities Management provides critical services to the college to ensure the safety of the students, faculty, and staff.  Facilities employees are critical personnel, which requires us to be present during inclement weather and all other emergencies . Marginal Job Functions: Contribute to the overall success of the department by performing all other essential duties and responsibilities as assigned. Education and Experience High School diploma or GED equivalent required. Journeyman license required. Valid driver’s license required. Three years of field experience in building maintenance related to heating, air conditioning and refrigeration system required. Valid license or certification of CFC, electrical or similar trade. Individual must possess or obtain a CFC license within a specified period. Knowledge and Skills General mechanical aptitude and the ability to solve complex mechanical problems on an emergency basis. Experience in copper brazing. Self motivated. Understanding of mechanical controls. Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Physical Requirements: Standing, walking, climbing stairs, ladders, turning, stooping, crouches and lifting heavy objects in excess of 50 pounds. Mobility on campus necessary.   Centre provides a supportive, engaging setting where faculty and staff thrive as we advance our shared mission: preparing students for lives of learning, leadership, and service. Join our community and leave a lasting impact on generations to come. As a fundamental policy and in compliance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and all other applicable non-discrimination laws, Centre College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or 